{"Title":"An Act authorizing the town of Acton to increase the residency limit for members of its police and fire departments","BillNumber":"H2657","DocketNumber":"HD2532","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"DAS1","Name":"Danillo A. Sena","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DAS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T14:23:56.583"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"DAS1","Name":"Danillo A. Sena","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DAS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T14:23:56.5833333"},{"Id":"S_C1","Name":"Simon Cataldo","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/S_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T14:26:30.9266667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2657/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Sena of Acton, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2657) of Danillo A. Sena and Simon Cataldo (by vote of the town) that the town of Acton be authorized to increase the residency limit for members of the police and fire departments of said town.  Public Service.  [Local Approval Received.]","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Notwithstanding section 99A of chapter 41 of the General Laws, or any other general or special law to the contrary, the town of Acton may increase the 15-mile residency limit contained in said section 99A of said chapter 41 for members of the Acton police and fire departments. Provided, that any increase in the residency limit shall be subject to a collective bargaining agreement negotiated in accordance with chapter 150E of the General Laws.\r\n\tSECTION 2. This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}